{"about_the_game":"<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Hollow Mire\u00a0- Shadow of Breken House\u00a0(Demo)</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Step into the opening chapters of <i>Hollow Mire</i>, a psychological mystery thriller set in post-war England.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This demo includes the <strong>prologue and first chapter</strong>, introducing war journalist <strong>John Rowe</strong> as he begins his assignment in the bleak English countryside. <br><br>After his encounter with a groundskeeper at a lonely train station, John arrives at the imposing <strong>Breken House</strong> on a dark, snow-laden night.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Inside its silent halls, shadows linger, secrets press close, and John\u2019s own struggles begin to surface. The mystery of Breken House begins.<br><br><strong>Read on discover more about the full game</strong><br>  <br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4036770/extras/89c5596a5e37c5bd1f3fa44b669dbe4d.webp?t=1762966560\" width=318 height=25 /></span>\u00a0 you've returned from the<strong> horrors of war</strong> to find your wife and daughter  missing. Years later, you're still searching. <br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline crossorigin=\"anonymous\" poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4036770/extras/d75d75b0b1102917787bace66e3c3fdc.poster.avif?t=1762966560\" width=780 height=438 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4036770/extras/d75d75b0b1102917787bace66e3c3fdc.webm?t=1762966560\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\"><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4036770/extras/8800433422e0d4932d4f8147983aaac5.webp?t=1762966560\" width=356 height=26 /></span>\u00a0c<strong>hasing the unexplained</strong>. With every story, you hold on to the hope that one day, something will lead you back to them.<br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline crossorigin=\"anonymous\" poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4036770/extras/603418e8274945a8458616dda905a03f.poster.avif?t=1762966560\" width=800 height=450 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4036770/extras/603418e8274945a8458616dda905a03f.webm?t=1762966560\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\"><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4036770/extras/7f6b406ee75d25f6fcac7cedfcaea2b2.webp?t=1762966560\" width=258 height=21 /></span>\u00a0takes you to '<strong>Breken House</strong>' in  England's snowy West Country. It feels familiar in a way that unsettles you, like you\u2019re finally close\u2026 or about to lose them all over again.<br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4036770/extras/f342607dffbdbd6d31427dc23e864c59.poster.avif?t=1762966560\" width=1170 height=658 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4036770/extras/f342607dffbdbd6d31427dc23e864c59.webm?t=1762966560\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4036770/extras/f342607dffbdbd6d31427dc23e864c59.mp4?t=1762966560\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\"></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\"><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4036770/extras/78239d62740f7a9541feb1585faee455.webp?t=1762966560\" width=326 height=40 /></span>\u00a0 <br>With <u><strong>8 unique endings</strong></u><strong>\u00a0-</strong>\u00a0Choose your words carefully  some decisions cannot be undone.  <br>  <br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4036770/extras/7dca3b935a10348beb2e52af65e8eb46.webp?t=1762966560\" width=414 height=42 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\">A fully voiced narrative experience, delivered by a professional cast.  <br>  <br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4036770/extras/6f165f7f17f2e3180d42042c61469153.webp?t=1762966560\" width=561 height=41 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\">John &amp; Gwen's stories weave together in the past and present  as does the <strong>consequences</strong> of their\u00a0your decisions.  <br>  <br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4036770/extras/7f625523fa644d60362ff8e51ee07391.webp?t=1762966560\" width=549 height=41 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\">Beautifully produced dark cello soundtrack supporting the game\u2019s themes of loss and memory, shifting between tension and sorrow, and rising to fear and action.  <br>  <br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4036770/extras/d9da74293532ae893ae6dc8f1ce509ac.webp?t=1762966560\" width=350 height=41 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\">Hollow Mire is inspired by <strong>themes of mid-20th century, England,</strong>\u00a0at a time when the country was recovering from war. A time before computers, before cell phones. Food rationing was still in effect and many families were coming to terms with the idea that many of the soldiers who went to Europe were never coming home.\u00a0 \u00a0<strong> </strong>     <br>     <br><strong>In 1952 a large blizzard swept across England</strong>, particularly impacting the West Country where Hollow Mire is set. The dark, snowy Devonshire Countryside is a truly beautiful and equally atmospheric place. It's quiet, lonely, dark and remote.        <br>     <br> You'll return to Normandy on <strong>June 6th 1944 (D-Day),</strong> seen as the turning point of the second World War. Part of the 9th Parachute Battalion, dropping behind enemy lines ahead of the main landings, and later visiting the camps.\u00a0        <br>     <br>Players should expect Hollow Mire to visit <strong>mature themes</strong> in some of the <strong>most difficult times in human history</strong>.\u00a0     <br>     <br>All environments are hand-painted with a focus on realism, a blend of Victorian and Edwardian architecture.    </p>","background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/4036770?t=1762966560","background_raw":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4036770/1aa074a2aba83dfd370221971eefd4810ecddb66/page_bg_raw.jpg?t=1762966560","capsule_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4036770/8c2ea16f9230c6a73bb8e3db7f9d459a6826863d/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1762966560","capsule_imagev5":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4036770/8c2ea16f9230c6a73bb8e3db7f9d459a6826863d/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1762966560","categories":[{"description":"Single-player","id":2},{"description":"Game demo","id":10},{"description":"Steam Achievements","id":22},{"description":"Full controller support","id":28},{"description":"Custom Volume Controls","id":68},{"description":"Keyboard Only Option","id":75},{"description":"Mouse Only Option","id":76},{"description":"Save Anytime","id":79}],"content_descriptors":{"ids":[],"notes":null},"controller_supp